   "value": "## Summary (2026-10-12, L = 2 pairs)\n\n- **Untwisted:** 𝒦 = left kernel of t̄₁(u) − t̄₃(u+h) has dim 136/256 (X(u) is linear in u). Product states in 𝒦 (40 random starts, all converge): **only the BPS orbit** (globally rotated vacua) — trivial, they see only the vacuum multiplet.\n- **Twisted, LR-compatible twist** Λ = diag(z₁, z₂, 1/z₂, 1/z₁) (z₁z₄ = z₂z₃ = 1; the t₃ twist detΛ·Λ⁻¹ is then the Weyl image of Λ): 36 of 256 eigenstates are LR symmetric and dim 𝒦^Λ = 36. The note's ⟨W_a^L| lies in 𝒦^Λ only for a = 0. Product states in 𝒦^Λ (60 starts, 45 reach f = 0): **only the four product eigenstates** e_a(A) ⊗ e_{5−a}(F) (vacuum and its Weyl images) — again trivial eigen-bras.\n- **So at L = 2 the LR-annihilated space contains no non-trivial factorised bra**, untwisted or with the LR-compatible diagonal twist. (Numerical search with random starts; 14 of the twisted starts stalled at local minima f ≈ 0.5, so isolated solutions cannot be excluded rigorously, but none was found.)\n- Not done: L = 3 (kernel at 4096 dims), non-diagonal LR-compatible twists, and allowing a relative constant c in t̄₁ − c·t̄₃(u+h) (here c = 1 is forced by the leading coefficients).",
